From a2edd7ffcd34426fe59d9c25c51220618f7da8ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stel777 <274792865+Stel777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 01:49:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] feat(graph,vaults): static graph mode + per-brain
 source folders
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Static graph: a third view mode beside 2D/3D that renders the 2D canvas
with the physics simulation frozen (cooldownTicks/warmupTicks 0, no
Three.js) at cached/settled node positions — full pan/zoom/hover/click,
much lower CPU for large graphs. Positions are captured on 2D
onEngineStop (localStorage) with a deterministic spiral fallback.

Source folders: each brain can be configured with external File-Explorer
folders it mirrors. A new source_mirror engine clones their *.md into the
vault under collision-safe <slug>/<rel> paths, tracks them in a per-brain
sources_manifest.json, ingests via the existing pipeline, and mirrors
deletions (removing the engram directly, since the vault watcher ignores
removes). Config persists in brains.json (never the rebuildable DB). The
file watcher also watches the source folders live; activation runs an
initial sync. New HTTP endpoints: GET/PUT /api/brains/:id/sources and
POST /api/brains/:id/sources/sync, with a management UI per brain card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
